{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>You shall no longer gather.</b> It is written with alef, and the custom is for it to be with vav, and both interchange with yod." "And the custom of builders of earth is to mix with it straw or stubble to make it stand." "<b>To brick.</b> From the root לבנה, and brick construction is stronger than stone construction, for earth construction water damages it, and stone construction fire damages it, and thus it is written: \"And brick served them as stone, and clay served them as mortar\" (Genesis 11:3). And know that there are nouns that have no meteg by virtue of their form at the etnaḥ or at the end of a verse, among those with kamatz katan like סֵפֶר (II Kings 5:5) and among those with pataḥ katan like צֶדֶק (Deuteronomy 1:16), and so too תבן, and their reason we do not know; only thus they are found." "<b>And you shall gather stubble.</b> From the root קש, of the doubled-root class."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:53.224753716Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}